{"availability":"available","full":"henningfutrell/hopper","name":"hopper","description":"Local job-queue daemon: pulls jobs from GitHub issues, runs them as Claude Code in herdr panes. Loopback only.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-05T16:12:55Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:59:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"dev","homepage":"https://henningfutrell.github.io/hopper/","topics":[],"demo":"https://henningfutrell.github.io/hopper/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.130Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.130Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.130Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:24.207Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:56.130Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A self-hosted job queue for coding agents. It pulls jobs from GitHub issues, runs each one as a Claude Code session in a herdr pane on a machine it manages, answers or escalates the questions a job asks, and keeps every machine inside its usage budget. One daemon, one Postgres database, a web UI, and an HTTP API with its reference at /docs/. Install page, step by step: (site/install.html). User guide, what it does with a job once it runs and what you can do: (site/guide.html).","the webhook subscriptions, all in that database and all edited in the UI; there is no config file. Secrets come from its environment.","machines, usage sources, notifiers (docs/plugins.md); the UI installs more from a plugin store."],"features":["Jobs are pulled, never pushed. A job is an issue with the hopper label, by an author you","Everything it keeps is in its database. Config is the plugins, rules and sign-in configs and","Every part is a plugin: router, queue sorter, escalation levels, executors, job sources,","Several people, kept apart. One hopper can work for several users: each has their own jobs,"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/henningfutrell/hoppe